162
00:37:36,966 --> 00:37:46,990
但是分母上的这个 $2$ 在二元域中是无意义的（因为 $2 = 0$ 无法作除数），而这个 2 正是来自配方法。 所以 $p = 2$ 是一个特例。
but this this $2$ is a nuisance if you're over the field of two elements, and that comes from completing the square.   So $p = 2$ is a special case.

163
00:37:46,990 --> 00:38:15,838
考察多项式 $x^2 + x + 1$。我断言它不可约。 为什么？因为它在 $\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}$ 中没有根。这个环中仅有的元素是 $0$ 和 $1$，要验证它没有根，只需代入 $0$ 和 $1$。
Take the polynomial $x^2 + x + 1$. I claim this is irreducible.   Why? Because it has no roots in $\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}$. The only elements in this ring are $0$ and $1$, so to see that it has no roots, you have to try $0$ and then you have to try $1$.

164
00:38:15,838 --> 00:38:22,645
如果代入$0$，得到 $0^2 + 0 + 1 = 1$；如果代入 $1$，得到 $1 + 1 + 1 = 1$。
If you try $0$, you get $0^2 + 0 + 1 = 1$; if you try $1$, you get $1 + 1 + 1 = 1$.

165
00:38:22,645 --> 00:38:35,270
因此该域中的任何元素代入都不等于 $0$，所以该多项式无根。 因为它的次数是 2，既然没有根，它就没有一次因式，因此它不可约！
So no substitution of an element in the field gives you $0$, so the polynomial has no roots.   Since it has degree 2, if it has no roots, it has no linear factors, therefore it's irreducible!

166
00:38:35,270 --> 00:38:51,680
于是你看：这就是具有 4 个元素的有限域，即 $(\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z})[x]$ 模去由 $x^2 + x + 1$ 生成的主理想。这是一个非常漂亮的乘法法则，通过处理溢出就能算出来。
So there you are: there's your field of four elements, $(\mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z})[x]$ modulo the ideal generated by $(x^2 + x + 1)$. That's a nice multiplication law to work out as you work out the overflow.

167
00:38:51,680 --> 00:39:19,387
好的，现在假设 $p > 2$。我们来考察这样一个多项式：$f(x) = x^2 - c$ 将是不可约的， 当且仅当 $c$ 不是$\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}$ 中的平方数，对吧？
Okay, now let's assume $p > 2$. So we're going to take a look at a polynomial like this: $f(x) = x^2 - c$ will be irreducible   if $c$ is not a square in $\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}$, right?

